e new  man the capitalists call it a  middle-income housing plan the New York  City Housing Authority becomes home to  five percent of the city's population  Britain's four million public sector  dwellings add to this mass housing  equation rivaling the Soviet bloc where  Khrushchev's uniform prefab concrete  slabs expand through multiplication from  Russia to Germany to Mongolia sixty  million people today still live in this  high-rise cornucopia publicly sponsored  housing isn't everywhere the diet beyond  Europe North America and the Soviet  Union high-rise development is rampantly  private except for Singapore Hong Kong  and isolated experiments such as Tata  loco in Mexico City with ancient Aztec  inheritance  the mass housing experiment is a  decade's long story of idealism and  destruction robert Moses's urban renewal  obliterates neighborhoods and boosts the  crime and segregation it claims to put  in reduction it leaves an often brutal  legacy take the Bronx air rights  building over yards of rail are the  bridge towers over a highway the noise  the fumes such an epic fail at ronan  point in the UK a prefab building is so  shoddily built it comes down on itself  taking with it five lives  the high-rise honeymoon is ending what  survives  alongside the vertical housing movement  a conflicting phenomenon urban sprawl  has matured the white middle-class flees  downtown on the highways planners such  as Robert Moses secured now many  high-rise neighborhoods instead of  housing this idealized middle-class have  become warehouses for their racialized  poor neglected by the state on mass the  building's fall apart from mismanagement  crime corruption and abandonment some  communities fight back now blaming the  buildings for the social failures  becomes the new credo the demolitions  begin here with the once admired st.  Louis's Pruitt Vigo down comes the  concrete Berlin Wall with it the Soviet  Union and its mass housing construction  sprawl yet in Singapore and